#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184010 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/id #uuid "fe8bd63f-87eb-5cc0-942c-011c3a59bc07" :question/math-academy-id "e-5063" :question/problem "Find the solution of $2x^2-6 \\le -4x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-6 & \\le -4x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+4x-6 & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x-3 & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=x^2+2x-3$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-3 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=1$ and $x=-3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/0fe5ab0d38cea340e2227157bf1d434a0fccbab153289db52106857530fbc4dc.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n\n$$\nx^2+2x-3 \\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis.  \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-3 \\le x \\le 1.$  \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x \\in [-3,1].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184012 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef5d4f19-5602-54a9-96ea-4e42054ff5c8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Greater Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "d992e18d-b1b0-536e-a3fd-c1e66fc72a30" :question/math-academy-id "e-5186" :question/problem "Find the solution of $x^2-2x-8 \\geq 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\nx^2-2x-8 \\geq 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=x^2-2x-8\n$$\n\nlies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/6e9eeff6caaad8efe92d4726c1f04175ed3023ea99b7990436597233ef2910df.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the axis or touches this axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x \\leq -2$ or $x \\geq 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184061 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Strict Quadratic Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/id #uuid "187f0c0b-6e70-5c17-800e-8bf4dad6d5be" :question/math-academy-id "e-9936" :question/problem "Find the solution of $2x^2 < -4x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2} & <-4x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+4x & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y = 2x^2 + 4x$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x = -2$ and $x = 0,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/936653d6efd2ff155768730d61af5b68924c48933fa81b77998a668b7691fa10.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n2x^2 + 4x \\lt 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2 < x < 0.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x \\in \\left(-2, 0\\right).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Less Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "9eee913a-b3ce-5268-aa2d-09f5e97b0700" :question/math-academy-id "e-9977" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny = -x^2 + 7 x - 10\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+7x-10 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-7x+10) & =0 \\\\ -(x-2)(x-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=2$ and $x = 5,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/13e108b6383e99c5840789389378fd58cd8704484296485cb6483112ecf4ae25.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x \\leq 2$ or $x \\geq 5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300496 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Strict Quadratic Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5b86b07-5152-5bfa-a7dd-3b1b2394348e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300498} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e0b446-5802-5c8b-b0b0-2e8f5ec099ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300499} {:answer/id #uuid "316cbeb6-9ef7-5ae8-aa88-f1613c80f372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300500} {:answer/id #uuid "3416eac5-8e06-514e-a69f-21acc3519d9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300501} {:answer/id #uuid "821f21a3-873e-51f8-bf21-d2513e077112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3416eac5-8e06-514e-a69f-21acc3519d9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300501} :answer-field/id #uuid "be4cc782-4666-5500-af79-b8103c59b4eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "292302ac-904d-59fe-b02a-d8afa13eb915" :question/math-academy-id "q-142177" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-5{x}^{2}>10x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5{x}^{2} & >10x \\\\ -5{x}^{2}-10x & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-5{x}^{2}-10x$ lies above the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5{x}^{2}-10x & =0 \\\\ -5x(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=-2,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/6cb044d4c6280d77dd525f6e2a8702d9fcba1553c2d33411407d69e09a6b715b.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-5{x}^{2}-10x>0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2<x<0.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-2,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef5d4f19-5602-54a9-96ea-4e42054ff5c8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Greater Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18af854d-5ad2-5e11-84b7-daace24e2618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le 3$ or $x\\ge 6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300505} {:answer/id #uuid "46686b94-fb93-5bd6-a55a-3d1e88237a98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3<x<6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300506} {:answer/id #uuid "641801e0-7e99-53e2-8a78-262737cc3391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\le x\\le 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300507} {:answer/id #uuid "af590961-0bd5-5ca1-a1b4-14fbac3432c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<3$ or $x>6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300508} {:answer/id #uuid "ea731b58-0672-5c27-9746-f4f563585cee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -6$ or $x\\ge -3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "641801e0-7e99-53e2-8a78-262737cc3391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\le x\\le 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300507} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2847316-26e8-5479-9c35-14bafbe0cd46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c874fa8-4e3f-5670-ad9f-092472b4f347" :question/math-academy-id "q-142180" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}+9x-18\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+9x-18\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}+9x-18\n$$\n\nlies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+9x-18 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-9x+18) & =0 \\\\ -(x-3)(x-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=3$ and $x=6,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/d4c28d26425c3c5bfc95dece73c8d8cb74f395f2de04a2c2ee1b1fd69f8433ed.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the axis or touches the $x$-axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $3\\le x\\le 6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Less Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b968ab7c-8cc3-5428-9d0f-13fe3fab9342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\le x\\le 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300512} {:answer/id #uuid "d790ffec-7049-513b-9e78-59a3039292a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -6$ or $x\\ge 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300513} {:answer/id #uuid "2781de1f-167c-5b66-afb0-cc59a101e459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le 1$ or $x\\ge 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300514} {:answer/id #uuid "dcb2bf41-1b26-552a-a9ff-495c9b6f3050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\le x\\le -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300515} {:answer/id #uuid "7b652b6d-5cac-5148-90b6-1ef7ad4d0d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -5$ or $x\\ge 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2781de1f-167c-5b66-afb0-cc59a101e459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le 1$ or $x\\ge 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300514} :answer-field/id #uuid "926e9b7a-b130-54b9-9210-d0d222f0a1f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f59dad02-8b17-598a-a754-71bfff242018" :question/math-academy-id "q-142315" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}+6x-5\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+6x-5\\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}+6x-5\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+6x-5 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-6x+5) & =0 \\\\ -(x-1)(x-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=1$ and $x=5,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/7cfa66b5aa6a3f29e7154e329926a47bbbb0eb45dce3251148986785f09ee383.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le 1$ or $x\\ge 5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef5d4f19-5602-54a9-96ea-4e42054ff5c8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Greater Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3005012d-3005-5574-841a-d6d8ef5f1cf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3005012d-3005-5574-841a-d6d8ef5f1cf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300519} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d56aba4-068f-554b-845b-6e41b8e9bedd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300518} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43b1c655-2664-5778-8256-7306ff56b09e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43b1c655-2664-5778-8256-7306ff56b09e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math