of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+6x\n$$\n\nlies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+6x & =0 \\\\ x(x+6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=-6,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/7d9fd824b1e4d63e417e002c07a01adb4c14f73fc81be66c31a5c9aa30ab7ffd.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le -6$ or $x\\ge 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Less Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91dd2a69-2949-5d2e-9dc5-bd3efda1032c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91dd2a69-2949-5d2e-9dc5-bd3efda1032c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300533} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ac4f0e-1fe9-5cb8-9d37-e82465603819" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc3e4819-7fdc-5daf-baf6-1a9240658f14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc3e4819-7fdc-5daf-baf6-1a9240658f14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300535} :answer-field/id #uuid "61d52ed9-bdc4-5cfc-ade4-71330dd7f5bb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5195263d-61c1-5000-8