swer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300540} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bfc3a8d-8388-5e63-9de0-d4f288e3d048" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300539} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0383579f-01ee-5c0e-bd91-1d0eef2a6d8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0383579f-01ee-5c0e-bd91-1d0eef2a6d8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300542} :answer-field/id #uuid "382dc4ea-c226-539a-bf4c-b9a0cd735211" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab62fed8-1fcd-5d99-8192-76b28169166e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab62fed8-1fcd-5d99-8192-76b28169166e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300544} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f31152-4a25-5926-b246-12a60329c9c2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8bf36c0-44b3-508f-92cd-90458542d6a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-277268" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}-5x<0.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$\\,\\text{or}\\,x>$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}-5x<0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}-5x\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-5x & =0 \\\\ -x(x+5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=-5,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/196587385ffa960d79d64d66f6ba14481905dd3de6159ecaec6a8e7bd2ab58b8.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<-5$ or $x>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cce52837-268a-5ecc-91da-5d71e8033de3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cce52837-268a-5ecc-91da-5d71e8033de3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300547} :answer-field/id #uuid "a72feb3f-0fe1-51e8-8a4e-89e35357811d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d3fbda6-0fb0-5b2d-8b8a-d3d0b50816fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d3fbda6-0fb0-5b2d-8b8a-d3d0b50816fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300549} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac47b8b5-23dd-5588-a2a7-16e6299fcb85" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300548} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008300ee-91bf-520b-8ee5-e9c2ac359303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "008300ee-91bf-520b-8ee5-e9c2ac359303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300551} :answer-field/id #uuid "512746bf-56cc-57f8-9cdf-a0ea75a34112" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06a5bdb6-75f8-585d-85f0-c921ed00a1b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-277446" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${x}^{2}\\ge 5x+14$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]\\,⋃\\,[$\n{{field-3}}$,\\,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\ge 5x+14 \\\\ {x}^{2}-5x-14 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-5x-14$ lies **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5x-14 & =0 \\\\ (x-7)(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=7,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/628325ae599d6b004fdabe85319ec9f8acd701c76b776cc4dea6b321cb554415.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-5x-14\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\le -2$ or $x\\ge 7.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-2]⋃[7,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300552 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Strict Quadratic Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f440c1d-110c-54ac-84b4-2a40cd3598f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300554} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbfbae5-eba9-5a3f-b48b-83a9c663c33f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fbfbae5-eba9-5a3f-b48b-83a9c663c33f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300555} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c140603-462d-5ff9-ab8a-5fa057ae2300" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d513bac4-354a-5d62-b24b-bf8b5e4f4e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d513bac4-354a-5d62-b24b-bf8b5e4f4e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300557} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7d52c53-503a-5a75-8622-540ec52e1798" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300556} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07462a1c-9a18-5910-b9ce-0940cfbb9c35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07462a1c-9a18-5910-b9ce-0940cfbb9c35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300559} :answer-field/id #uuid "2176a80e-cd5b-5ea6-b594-7d0a0b8d955d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36c23665-56f9-5a18-9dfe-701a3d244591" :question/math-academy-id "q-277664" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${x}^{2}>12x$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\,⋃\\,(${{field-3}}$,\\,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & >12x \\\\ {x}^{2}-12x & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-12x$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-12x & =0 \\\\ x(x-12) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=12,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/387b02ad3416b06b3f86f12c99b921800ab4b86f39be9da0fc48883952d366d2.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-12x>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x<0$ or $x>12.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,0)⋃(12,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300560 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Strict Quadratic Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2213bcde-f411-52e7-89d5-75c0d9453f8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2213bcde-f411-52e7-89d5-75c0d9453f8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300562} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf39dc5c-a856-5b78-a9f5-723f472e4485" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300561} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c57b760c-2f49-5596-b1a7-e36f9eb8cb8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c57b760c-2f49-5596-b1a7-e36f9eb8cb8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300564} :answer-field/id #uuid "1481635d-90cb-50f3-a54d-91682e323b61" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e3b29a5b-bbb4-5fb4-8d0f-7a1a962e9cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-277670" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-{x}^{2}>-x-12$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2} & >-x-12 \\\\ -{x}^{2}+x+12 & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-{x}^{2}+x+12$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+x+12 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-x-12) & =0 \\\\ -(x+3)(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-3$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/32e9a7babfbe9132a3a3e18c2f1efcbc3a33cd59bccc02099c7045b3fc39ee75.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+x+12>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-3<x<4.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-3,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Strict Quadratic Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c404b6a-96c5-5345-b717-148acadd2c70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300567} {:answer/id #uuid "c85749d4-d1f2-5db6-98ee-f36b3d2c06ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c85749d4-d1f2-5db6-98ee-f36b3d2c06ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300568} :answer-field/id #uuid "472af46d-1570-5103-b2d3-1862fb2b88cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300566} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaad5350-323d-5306-93ad-8cd509b20e91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaad5350-323d-5306-93ad-8cd509b20e91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300570} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb82d6e-411e-56d8-a96e-bd0990c0cebe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0f81b704-2a60-5224-96b8-0941c805eb95" :question/math-academy-id "q-277671" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-2{x}^{2}>10x+12$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2} & >10x+12 \\\\ -2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}-10x-12$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+10x+12 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+6x)+(4x+12) & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+3)+4(x+3) & =0 \\\\ (2x+4)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-3$ and $x=-2,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/539e0e68f4a03c0bd4a309ebf2c4a00638d99c6eee233ca8f2cef3814e419c95.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}-10x-12>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-3<x<-2.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-3,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef486d5b-856b-5e96-a823-26277781df64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,9]\\cup [0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300573} {:answer/id #uuid "557bf362-c269-5faa-b5e9-d2b620a376f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-9,9]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300574} {:answer/id #uuid "688f528a-2a4d-5a1d-b1c7-33237de89fea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-9,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300575} {:answer/id #uuid "3152fd5f-053a-53ef-b4b5-f23db7077658" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,9]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300576} {:answer/id #uuid "066c2e89-73b8-5bcf-923c-00f96ba2cf9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-9]\\cup [0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "688f528a-2a4d-5a1d-b1c7-33237de89fea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-9,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300575} :answer-field/id #uuid "a183b333-0b28-5416-8dbd-17b595d42844" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30b6a93f-c7e8-5ae1-bd52-e140f18d4ecf" :question/math-academy-id "q-3875" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}\\le -9x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\le -9x \\\\ {x}^{2}+9x & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}+9x$ lies below the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+9x & =0 \\\\ x(x+9) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-9$ and $x=0,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/eacd8f468f34bea6eec93afd32bbeee452a3a6435342035f7c45c3578f40f92f.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+9x\\le 0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-9\\le x\\le 0.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-9,0].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Strict Quadratic Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be09d222-128e-5ae7-ae14-5d658832c8f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300580} {:answer/id #uuid "81296db2-a25c-59ea-897c-e682c8e58487" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300581} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e02b04-a58f-5f09-97ad-641ac954cf2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300582} {:answer/id #uuid "a57fbec7-0f7f-5037-a549-88779863bb31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300583} {:answer/id #uuid "37bc8824-4184-56a9-b61c-eb8af36c361d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81296db2-a25c-59ea-897c-e682c8e58487" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300581} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ddb46e4-0104-553a-bac1-eec771025c8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1cef3625-3cc4-5826-9ae1-374c64937713" :question/math-academy-id "q-3878" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}<3x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & <3x \\\\ {x}^{2}-3x & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-3x$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-3x & =0 \\\\ x(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/a341979142ef569d7ba4ec5b44178e8b4e4374fa9294e4664ae0f0008b76caab.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-3x<0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0<x<3.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (0,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300585 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491d4207-815d-51c2-b0d2-c5bb36a643af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-4,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300587} {:answer/id #uuid "42a70efb-e811-59ca-8b82-7d0822752496" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4]\\cup [0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300588} {:answer/id #uuid "42b5bcb4-ae97-5343-bd13-69bf3de6d303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-4,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300589} {:answer/id #uuid "96aeab05-8205-5ad4-a837-aae1365e97b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300590} {:answer/id #uuid "1ff8c155-e111-5f11-a27b-95d67ef2d45a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0]\\cup [4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96aeab05-8205-5ad4-a837-aae1365e97b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300590} :answer-field/id #uuid "31c95dd9-6725-56ed-8818-45591275d67d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa538d2c-daa6-561a-b09f-00677fd2938c" :question/math-academy-id "q-3881" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}\\ge -4x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2} & \\ge -4x \\\\ -{x}^{2}+4x & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-{x}^{2}+4x$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ -x(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/d234c29de2a39c664d6a03acf1d8cc43782914a3c82045cc103353ebaf67b897.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+4x\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0\\le x\\le 4.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [0,4].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89132c69-3565-5bf2-857b-18937f1dfa5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [- 1, \\frac{8}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183150} {:answer/id #uuid "95755705-5578-5ef9-82ba-43457bf7b2f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [- 4, \\frac{3}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183151} {:answer/id #uuid "1d11c011-de09-52b4-9385-2ca2f82c367b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [- \\frac{1}{2}, 2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183152} {:answer/id #uuid "379d3b51-8701-523b-ad2d-ec5933cd9ccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [0, 2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183153} {:answer/id #uuid "4e9e0643-632f-5442-aba3-118bf6c32753" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [\\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{11}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95755705-5578-5ef9-82ba-43457bf7b2f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [- 4, \\frac{3}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183151} :answer-field/id #uuid "627c9fc9-38d6-5bba-a662-7cea5af01656" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183149}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9eaa518b-95b3-5d3f-9f89-7edbce2847db" :question/math-academy-id "q-3951" :question/problem "Find the solution of $2{x}^{2}-12\\le -5x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-12 & \\le -5x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+5x-12 & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=2{x}^{2}+5x-12$ lies below the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+5x-12 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+8x)+(-3x-12) & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+4)-3(x+4) & =0 \\\\ (2x-3)(x+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/ba6c384800a5b42f2033527997328aa9f9d792b33b3fabecfe9b3a93789f46c4.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n \n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+5x-12\\le 0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\n Based on the graph, the solution is $-4\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-4,\\frac{3}{2}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77d4cc90-88df-5703-b111-000a78f60eb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{2}]\\cup [0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300594} {:answer/id #uuid "f91c9c34-345a-509a-8d6e-6a9058bd4cd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,\\frac{5}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300595} {:answer/id #uuid "c3505a1b-80dc-5a09-b7f4-2a9347db1405" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0]\\cup [\\frac{5}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300596} {:answer/id #uuid "4fe6323b-1275-5ee6-a278-aeaa86cf5d14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300597} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1bb29a-3d57-5742-b1d7-fb6c5aaa73af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f1bb29a-3d57-5742-b1d7-fb6c5aaa73af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300598} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8606a1e-4f71-50a8-9377-1ebe62b5ce95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e00f75b4-33fd-550f-8d24-3fa586937e86" :question/math-academy-id "q-44772" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-2{x}^{2}\\ge 5x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2} & \\ge 5x \\\\ -2{x}^{2}-5x & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}-5x$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-5x & =0 \\\\ -x(2x+5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $x=0,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/33b031b579d84d633e4dcc56c912333327449fcbc6969eeceb34e209c4d308d1.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}-5x\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\n Based on the graph, the solution is $-\\frac{5}{2}\\le x\\le 0.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},0].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef5d4f19-5602-54a9-96ea-4e42054ff5c8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Greater Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "975a7326-d34f-5716-80c3-4c09e9a0188e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x \\le 0$ or $x \\ge 3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183552} {:answer/id #uuid "d39996f1-9e8e-579d-92e2-5d67861bf5cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3 \\le x \\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183553} {:answer/id #uuid "f33f84e5-bb26-58cb-b820-f406c5bca8a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3 \\le x \\le 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183554} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbe254d-980f-5e1b-93d4-63387ead9a8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x \\le - 3$ or $x \\ge 0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183555} {:answer/id #uuid "6f9ea5a9-bf8d-5525-9f81-656030d3f808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0 \\le x \\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f9ea5a9-bf8d-5525-9f81-656030d3f808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0 \\le x \\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183556} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ab5b6a2-f335-59b2-831a-2eb686fbaa7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "016ffd75-b70d-57d9-8a72-260ee474836b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70302" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}+3x\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+3x\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}+3x\n$$\n\nlies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+3x & =0 \\\\ -x(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/68d82c96c820a6a0bf5e3c74ea93cbf2091e96ebfa7dfe200e8beb140cb7962e.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the axis or touches the $x$-axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $0\\le x\\le 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Less Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ff80692-da9c-5a78-96fd-857b3061bfec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<-3$ or $x>1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300601} {:answer/id #uuid "820bafa6-fd41-5980-80f5-9428fda86f70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3<x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300602} {:answer/id #uuid "12b117f9-be8d-5233-a413-1b4992519d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3<x<3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300603} {:answer/id #uuid "5ddfafa3-cab3-5c67-b75a-b93000be8163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x<3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300604} {:answer/id #uuid "248e656b-e729-508a-858e-603a397ae85a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<0$ or $x>3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ff80692-da9c-5a78-96fd-857b3061bfec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<-3$ or $x>1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300601} :answer-field/id #uuid "8684e7df-b19d-512b-bfac-7e235aa7007d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ab8c812-0c5a-5955-8938-c9f15da2c8e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-70303" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}-2x+3<0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}-2x+3<0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}-2x+3\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-2x+3 & =0 \\\\ -(x-1)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-3$ and $x=1,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/289eed0e3b3047987dfbc729d0c22af32d1297ed2fb2d564ec725868b92a39c1.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<-3$ or $x>1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Less Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7ecba10-7014-5d9f-89fa-7a75ac217884" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1<x<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300608} {:answer/id #uuid "a1379be3-73d3-51ca-af0a-6290a0089ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<-1$ or $x>4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300609} {:answer/id #uuid "07eb0954-a1e1-5d94-9675-9f1bc950730e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<x<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300610} {:answer/id #uuid "f9348b10-975f-533c-bba1-f6eb88c320fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<-4$ or $x>1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300611} {:answer/id #uuid "498661af-346b-56a2-8c7b-370f33fdc44e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4<x<1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9348b10-975f-533c-bba1-f6eb88c320fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<-4$ or $x>1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300611} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad67f50-8bb3-56ff-9c56-7d0da4b137b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ed431b7-d26a-5c50-bd2b-a4420875bdfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-75991" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}-3x+4<0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}-3x+4<0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}-3x+4\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-3x+4 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}+3x-4) & =0 \\\\ -(x+4)(x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=1,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/6a5528147c994e180c2ffb41bd259dae489a3fc02fa1d6c77452d6cf1722e9be.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<-4$ or $x>1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300613 